    description: "When changing tracker item status, it's natural to want to add a note explaining why in the same command. Currently requires two commands:\n  scripts/tracker update FOO --status done\n  scripts/tracker discuss FOO \"Implemented in PR #1234\"\n\nProposal: Add --note flag to update subcommand as syntactic sugar:\n  scripts/tracker update FOO --status done --note \"Implemented in PR #1234\"\n\nImplementation: When --note is provided, append it as a discussion entry (same as calling discuss) after the status update. No schema changes needed — just an alias for the discuss subcommand triggered within update.\n\nMotivation: META-radiz context was lost when the agent tried --note (which didn't exist), got an error, retried without it, and moved on without using discuss as a fallback."  # b003
    fields: {}  # b003
